──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SURFACE PARITY — what was ported from the web source (no scope narrowing)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
• Composition : the always-on footer (web `<footer role="status" aria-live="polite">`) with the leading group
                (Connection · divider · Live telemetry) and the trailing group (Background work · Active
                vehicle · divider · Help · divider · Version) — every region of StatusBar.tsx + its 6 segments.
• Prefs       : web `useStatusBarPrefs`/`setStatusBarPrefs` (localStorage + cross-tab sync) → a `@MainActor`
                StatusBarPrefsStore seam (P1/S8) with a UserDefaults impl (same `teslasync-status-bar-prefs`
                key) + an in-memory test impl; `!enabled` → the view renders nothing (web `return null`);
                `iconOnly = compact || prefs.iconOnly || isNarrow` (web `useNarrowViewport`).
• Connection  : web `useApiHealth` → ok/degraded/offline/unknown, each pairing a tone (positive/caution/
                critical/neutral → status tokens) with a DISTINCT SF Symbol + dot (color never the sole
                encoder), the "API" label, the latency chip (hidden offline/unknown), the "· Offline" suffix,
                tooltip + aria; opens /system-status.
• Live        : web `useLiveConnection` → connected/reconnecting/disconnected/unknown + the native `stale`
                (ADR-013), the spinning glyph while reconnecting (Reduce-Motion-aware), the periodic
                last-message age (ageSecondsLabel ported s/m/h); opens /signal-diff.
• Vehicle     : web `useSelectedVehicle` + `useVehicleState` → hidden (0 cars) / static chip (1) / popover
                switcher (2+); the `display_name || vin || "Vehicle {id}" || "No vehicle"` fallback; the
                "{battery}% · {range} {unit}" chip (convertDistanceFromSI ported, m→km/mi + round).
• Background  : web `useBackgroundJobs` → hidden when idle, else a spinner + "{count} task(s)" opening a jobs
                popover (export/mutation/custom glyphs, "Running" heading, per-job label + detail).
• Help        : web `HelpSegment` → keyboard-shortcuts (?-keycap) / take-a-tour / report-bug, each routed to
                a bound StatusBarCommands intent (the web window-event dispatches).
• Version     : web `VersionSegment` → version + git SHA (dev sentinel hidden), update / unseen-changelog
                dots, the About-this-build sheet (web `Modal`) with the provenance rows (app version, commit,
                helm chart, Go runtime, platform os/arch join, server uptime — uptimeLabel ported), the
                update banner, and the changelog / release-notes / close actions.
• States      : loading (skeleton chrome) + the orthogonal offline / stale / error chips (cached-on-offline,
                freshness chip + one-shot stale rising-edge auto-refresh, backend-unreachable + retry) +
                empty (0 vehicles + 0 jobs → Help+Version remain, never a blank box) — the full P4 contract,
                faithful to a presentational bar whose data lives in its segments.
• i18n        : 100% via the P1/S10 facade (StatusBarStrings, table "StatusBar"); 55 keys, a perfect 1:1
                match between StatusBar.strings and the keys referenced in code (verified by diff; the only
                code key absent from the catalog is the intentional `any.key` absent-key test probe). Zero
                English literals in Swift beyond the web-default fallbacks. i18next `{{age/count/uptime}}` →
                StatusBarInterpolation.
• Telemetry   : P1/S11 `view.opened` emitted exactly once with surface slug "StatusBar".
• a11y        : VoiceOver labels on every interactive element (connection, live, vehicle switcher + each
                option, background popover, 3 help buttons, version, retry); the footer carries the `status`
                label + `updatesFrequently` trait (web aria-live polite); Dynamic Type via Font.TS roles;
                Reduce-Motion-aware spinners + skeleton shimmer.
• Architecture: pure Adapter/SegmentModels/Projection/Resolve/ResolveVersion/Copy (Sendable, SwiftUI-free,
                unit-tested) → Prefs + Model (P1/S8 store + command seams, P1/S11 telemetry seam, P1/S10
                facade, @Observable @MainActor) → swift/Segments/Popovers/Version/States (P1/S9 tokens only;
                no direct library imports, no networking, no raw hex).

